<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46461" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suf-fŭgĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subf-</span></b> ), fūgi,
		3, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to flee away</i> (rare;
			not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">custodes vigilesque suffugere in tecta
					coëgit (imber),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 46</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to flee from</i>, <i>to shun</i>, <i>avoid</i>, <i>escape</i> a person or thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manuum tactum et ictum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 150</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sensum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					360</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consularem orare conantem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 27</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
